1
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:13,250
I am the bone of my sword.

2
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:17,499
Steel is my body,
and fire is my blood.

3
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:19,880
I have created over
a thousand blades.

4
00:00:20,670 --> 00:00:23,169
Unknown to Death,

5
00:00:23,170 --> 00:00:25,260
nor known to Life.

6
00:00:26,550 --> 00:00:31,100
Have withstood pain to
create many weapons.

7
00:00:32,770 --> 00:00:34,940
Yet, those hands will
never hold anything.

8
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:41,400
So as I pray,
Unlimited Blade Works.

9
00:01:07,010 --> 00:01:11,310
So that's how he
became a Heroic Spirit.

10
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:14,020
What an idiot.

11
00:01:27,150 --> 00:01:32,190
In the face of absolute despair

12
00:01:32,490 --> 00:01:36,190
That nearly burned
our hearts away

13
00:01:37,690 --> 00:01:42,740
You still found the
courage to smile

14
00:01:42,990 --> 00:01:47,540
Like you accepted it all

15
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:50,800
I lost my voice

16
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,420
And the things I wanted to say

17
00:01:53,700 --> 00:01:58,670
But every time I
fell to my knees

18
00:01:59,020 --> 00:02:02,970
I stood up and kept walking

19
00:02:03,240 --> 00:02:08,640
We were looking for
the ideal white future

20
00:02:08,850 --> 00:02:13,870
Our one and only hope

21
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:16,360
Now I may be left with nothing

22
00:02:16,530 --> 00:02:21,780
But these raging
emotions that have

23
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:24,880
Nowhere to go

24
00:02:25,130 --> 00:02:30,130
Still, I'll look for a new dawn

25
00:02:30,510 --> 00:02:33,540
With more than one right answer

26
00:02:33,780 --> 00:02:37,370
I won't stop

27
00:02:37,670 --> 00:02:39,400
Until I find it

28
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:48,690
How long do you intend
to keep playing around?

29
00:02:48,691 --> 00:02:49,880
The Fifth Contractor

30
00:02:49,881 --> 00:02:51,359
Huh? Just until 7:30.

31
00:02:51,360 --> 00:02:53,450
Any longer, and I'll
be late for school.

32
00:02:54,030 --> 00:02:56,789
I wasn't referring to
your leaving for school.

33
00:02:56,790 --> 00:03:00,000
I was referring to
the Holy Grail War.

34
00:03:00,870 --> 00:03:03,709
Cooperating with another
Master isn't a bad idea.

35
00:03:03,710 --> 00:03:07,710
But you've chosen the worst
possible partner you could.

36
00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:13,889
Didn't I say I wouldn't break
my pact with Emiya-kun?

37
00:03:13,890 --> 00:03:16,389
I admit he isn't
much use in a fight,

38
00:03:16,390 --> 00:03:18,600
but I have no complaints
with him as an ally.

39
00:03:19,470 --> 00:03:20,980
I mean...

40
00:03:21,390 --> 00:03:25,020
I feel like Emiya-kun would
never betray me, no matter what.

41
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:27,569
Listen.

42
00:03:27,570 --> 00:03:29,940
That boy isn't a winner.

43
00:03:30,610 --> 00:03:34,240
If you must ally with someone,
even Caster would be better.

44
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:37,159
Don't be absurd, Archer.

45
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:41,250
Are you telling me to take a
common stance with that monster?

46
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:50,920
Yes, she is a monster, but
she behaves like a real mage.

47
00:03:51,590 --> 00:03:54,969
And if you too are a mage, you
should prioritize results over ideals.

48
00:03:54,970 --> 00:03:58,970
Your snide remarks won't work. I
don't intend to change my position.

49
00:03:59,510 --> 00:04:02,599
What in the world
has gotten into you?

50
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:05,979
You've been acting strangely ever
since you got to know Emiya Shirou.

51
00:04:05,980 --> 00:04:08,320
What happened to your
detached rationality?

52
00:04:08,940 --> 00:04:12,069
Yes, I know I'm not myself.

53
00:04:12,070 --> 00:04:17,819
But that's all because of the
nonsense you've been showing me.

54
00:04:17,820 --> 00:04:18,820
What?

55
00:04:19,410 --> 00:04:21,160
It's nothing. Forget it.

56
00:04:21,750 --> 00:04:24,642
Anyway, since you're
my Servant, bear in

57
00:04:24,654 --> 00:04:27,920
mind that I'll only do
what I think is right.

58
00:04:28,460 --> 00:04:31,759
I'm not as naïve
as Emiya Shirou,

59
00:04:31,760 --> 00:04:33,630
but there are some
things I won't budge on.

60
00:04:34,470 --> 00:04:37,760
I won't compromise on
those—not for anyone.

61
00:04:38,510 --> 00:04:40,140
What do you say to that, Archer?

62
00:04:43,180 --> 00:04:44,770
What can I say?

63
00:04:47,310 --> 00:04:51,650
It's a vassal's duty to support
his lord when she's out of sorts.

64
00:04:53,030 --> 00:04:56,950
I'll watch over you from the
shadows until you're yourself again.

65
00:05:11,340 --> 00:05:12,879
What's wrong with me?

66
00:05:12,880 --> 00:05:15,420
I've been waking
up exhausted lately.

67
00:05:18,840 --> 00:05:21,640
Well, those really
were beautiful swords.

68
00:05:22,310 --> 00:05:23,520
Yeah, that's right.

69
00:05:24,890 --> 00:05:27,310
I like them. Is that so bad?

70
00:05:31,650 --> 00:05:33,280
That's all I had to tell you.

71
00:05:33,780 --> 00:05:35,736
Also, I'm sure I don't
need to remind you

72
00:05:35,748 --> 00:05:37,860
of this, but don't
forget to lock the doors.

73
00:05:38,150 --> 00:05:40,870
Of course. That
goes without saying.

74
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:48,120
Hey, Issei.

75
00:05:48,670 --> 00:05:50,079
What is it, Emiya?

76
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:52,879
I've been curious
about this for a while.

77
00:05:52,880 --> 00:05:55,799
Are you and Kuzuki close?

78
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:58,549
Oh, I guess I never
told you, did I?

79
00:05:58,550 --> 00:06:00,800
It's only natural that
we'd be on good terms.

80
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:05,849
After all, he's like a
surrogate big brother to me.

81
00:06:05,850 --> 00:06:07,020
A big brother?

82
00:06:08,350 --> 00:06:10,519
Souichirou—no,

83
00:06:10,520 --> 00:06:14,979
Kuzuki-sensei has been staying at
the temple for the past three years or so.

84
00:06:14,980 --> 00:06:20,110
He's the quiet type, but he's
a forthright and sincere man.

85
00:06:20,820 --> 00:06:24,620
My respect for him is based on
our living under the same roof.

86
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:27,440
It's only natural that I should
look up to him as a brother.

87
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:30,620
Kuzuki lives at Ryuudou Temple?

88
00:06:34,340 --> 00:06:35,050
Wha...

89
00:06:35,051 --> 00:06:37,630
Tohsaka?

90
00:06:38,010 --> 00:06:41,129
Student Council President, while we're on
the topic of this "big brother" of yours...

91
00:06:41,130 --> 00:06:43,390
Has anything happened
at the temple recently?

92
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:48,349
I have nothing to say to someone
who'd stoop to eavesdropping!

93
00:06:48,350 --> 00:06:50,389
Issei, I'd like to know as well.

94
00:06:50,390 --> 00:06:53,269
Wh-What's going on with you two?

95
00:06:53,270 --> 00:06:54,980
Especially after
the other day...

96
00:06:57,780 --> 00:07:00,819
Well, I suppose one
thing comes to mind.

97
00:07:00,820 --> 00:07:03,950
Kuzuki-sensei is
getting married soon.

98
00:07:04,820 --> 00:07:09,160
About two weeks ago, he brought home a
woman whom he introduced as his fiancée.

99
00:07:09,910 --> 00:07:14,330
Although it does strike me as
a bit odd, I'm happy for them.

100
00:07:14,630 --> 00:07:17,299
We've given her special
permission to stay there.

101
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:20,300
They're living together in quarters
separate from the main temple for now.

102
00:07:23,930 --> 00:07:24,930
We've found him.

103
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:27,599
After what happened with Issei,

104
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:31,979
I think it's crazy to suspect someone
just because they live at Ryuudou Temple.

105
00:07:31,980 --> 00:07:33,019
Why?

106
00:07:33,020 --> 00:07:35,770
He couldn't be more suspicious.
He must be the Master.

107
00:07:36,270 --> 00:07:38,819
That "fiancée" of his is Caster.

108
00:07:38,820 --> 00:07:39,900
There's no doubt.

109
00:07:40,320 --> 00:07:42,109
We attack tonight.

110
00:07:42,110 --> 00:07:43,739
Emiya-kun, you
should go prepare too.

111
00:07:43,740 --> 00:07:45,119
Hang on.

112
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:46,120
Tonight?

113
00:07:46,320 --> 00:07:47,779
Of course.

114
00:07:47,780 --> 00:07:51,749
There's no guarantee that Kuzuki-sensei
will come to school tomorrow.

115
00:07:51,750 --> 00:07:54,789
We'll test him on his way
home to see if he's a Master.

116
00:07:54,790 --> 00:07:57,250
Test him? How?

117
00:07:59,630 --> 00:08:01,420
I'll hit him with a
light Gandr shot.

118
00:08:02,010 --> 00:08:06,260
Even if Kuzuki-sensei's a normal person,
he'll only end up bedridden for a few days.

119
00:08:06,850 --> 00:08:08,849
That doesn't work either.

120
00:08:08,850 --> 00:08:12,519
If he is a Master, it'll turn
into a fight then and there.

121
00:08:12,520 --> 00:08:14,350
And then it'll be
too late to talk it out.

122
00:08:15,770 --> 00:08:18,269
But that'd be all
the better for us.

123
00:08:18,270 --> 00:08:19,520
What's the problem?

124
00:08:20,070 --> 00:08:23,950
Well, if that happens,
you'll be in danger.

125
00:08:24,490 --> 00:08:26,699
Oh, I don't really mind.

126
00:08:26,700 --> 00:08:29,160
I'll just handle him myself.

127
00:08:29,910 --> 00:08:30,950
Jeez.

128
00:08:32,540 --> 00:08:34,960
Fine. I'll go with you.

129
00:08:37,460 --> 00:08:40,460
Then you intend to attack
Caster's Master tonight?

130
00:08:40,800 --> 00:08:45,589
Yeah. We still don't know for certain
that Kuzuki-sensei's the Master,

131
00:08:45,590 --> 00:08:47,470
but at this point, we'll
just have to test him.

132
00:08:48,090 --> 00:08:49,509
That's true.

133
00:08:49,510 --> 00:08:52,099
I understand your
reluctance, Shirou.

134
00:08:52,100 --> 00:08:54,140
But for now, let us go
along with Rin's plan.

135
00:09:03,820 --> 00:09:06,700
I wish I could fight
more like he does.

136
00:09:11,330 --> 00:09:12,830
What am I thinking?

137
00:09:38,650 --> 00:09:43,529
When I called Fuji-nee—no,
Fujimura-sensei just now to check,

138
00:09:43,530 --> 00:09:46,069
she said Kuzuki
hadn't left school yet.

139
00:09:46,070 --> 00:09:49,529
Which means that he's still
following his usual routine tonight.

140
00:09:49,530 --> 00:09:52,240
In which case, he'll be
leaving school any time now.

141
00:09:54,910 --> 00:09:57,960
Rin, why is Archer not here?

142
00:09:58,670 --> 00:10:01,079
I left him at home.

143
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:04,299
I don't want him around Caster.

144
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:05,460
What does that mean?

145
00:10:07,510 --> 00:10:08,550
Let's hurry.

146
00:10:14,810 --> 00:10:17,559
It's a straight road from
here to Ryuudou Temple,

147
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:20,059
so Kuzuki will
definitely pass this spot.

148
00:10:20,060 --> 00:10:22,650
We'll set our trap
here and ambush him.

149
00:10:23,270 --> 00:10:25,020
It's an ideal location,
don't you think?

150
00:10:25,730 --> 00:10:27,899
It's nothing fancy, but I
can set up a magic field here

151
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:31,910
to completely soundproof the
area, though we'll still be visible.

152
00:10:32,410 --> 00:10:35,739
A missile could blow this place sky
high and no one would hear a thing.

153
00:10:35,740 --> 00:10:36,829
Well?

154
00:10:36,830 --> 00:10:37,910
Excellent work.

155
00:10:38,250 --> 00:10:40,919
Okay, Saber, as
for the plan itself...

156
00:10:40,920 --> 00:10:41,920
Tohsaka!

157
00:10:42,250 --> 00:10:43,710
Looks like he's here.

158
00:10:55,970 --> 00:11:00,140
Hey, Tohsaka. I'm
thinking it really isn't Kuzuki.

159
00:11:00,640 --> 00:11:03,400
Well, we'll know
once we do this.

160
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:05,900
Here goes.

161
00:11:14,120 --> 00:11:15,120
Wait.

162
00:11:16,780 --> 00:11:19,370
I thought I warned
you, Souichirou.

163
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:25,290
This was bound to happen, so you
should have remained at Ryuudou Temple.

164
00:11:26,710 --> 00:11:27,920
I wouldn't say that.

165
00:11:29,300 --> 00:11:32,220
After all, we have
caught our prey.

166
00:11:46,810 --> 00:11:50,820
Now, come on out,
foolish little mage.

167
00:11:51,400 --> 00:11:53,029
I shall give you three seconds.

168
00:11:53,030 --> 00:11:58,080
After that, I shall respond
in kind to your aggression.

169
00:11:58,490 --> 00:12:00,869
Emiya-kun, are you ready?

170
00:12:00,870 --> 00:12:02,869
When I give the
signal, we start.

171
00:12:02,870 --> 00:12:03,959
Sorry.

172
00:12:03,960 --> 00:12:06,209
Save that for later, Tohsaka.

173
00:12:06,210 --> 00:12:07,210
Huh?

174
00:12:07,670 --> 00:12:08,670
Shirou!

175
00:12:14,430 --> 00:12:16,339
Well, this is a surprise.

176
00:12:16,340 --> 00:12:20,179
I see you've grown a little
smarter since I last saw you, boy.

177
00:12:20,180 --> 00:12:22,679
Tohsaka and Emiya?

178
00:12:22,680 --> 00:12:26,559
So it isn't only Matou. You
two are Masters as well.

179
00:12:26,560 --> 00:12:29,440
You may be mages,
but it is still unfortunate.

180
00:12:29,770 --> 00:12:33,280
Kuzuki, are you being
controlled by Caster?

181
00:12:33,570 --> 00:12:35,529
You're such an irritating boy...

182
00:12:35,530 --> 00:12:37,449
Perhaps I shall kill you.

183
00:12:37,450 --> 00:12:38,450
Wait.

184
00:12:38,950 --> 00:12:42,539
What makes you ask
that question, Emiya?

185
00:12:42,540 --> 00:12:45,119
There must be a reason
why you'd suspect so.

186
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:46,669
Tell me.

187
00:12:46,670 --> 00:12:49,090
You're a decent
human being, right?

188
00:12:49,710 --> 00:12:53,590
You couldn't possibly be turning
a blind eye to what Caster's doing.

189
00:12:54,380 --> 00:12:57,219
What Caster is doing?

190
00:12:57,220 --> 00:12:58,509
Yeah.

191
00:12:58,510 --> 00:13:01,850
Caster's taking mana
from people all across town.

192
00:13:02,220 --> 00:13:05,440
To her, humans are
no more than sacrifices.

193
00:13:06,390 --> 00:13:09,189
As long as Caster
keeps draining people,

194
00:13:09,190 --> 00:13:11,520
it's only a matter of time
before she kills someone.

195
00:13:12,320 --> 00:13:16,450
Before long, she'll have done
something that can't be fixed.

196
00:13:16,780 --> 00:13:17,989
I understand.

197
00:13:17,990 --> 00:13:22,409
You think that I, her Master,
was permitting her actions

198
00:13:22,410 --> 00:13:25,790
because I was under her control.

199
00:13:26,250 --> 00:13:30,630
Yeah. So if that's the case,
we'll only defeat Caster.

200
00:13:30,960 --> 00:13:35,339
But if you gave Caster free
rein, knowing what she was up to,

201
00:13:35,340 --> 00:13:37,260
that makes you no
more than a killer.

202
00:13:37,840 --> 00:13:39,470
And I won't show
you mercy, either.

203
00:13:47,770 --> 00:13:50,770
No, this is the first
I've heard of this.

204
00:13:52,610 --> 00:13:54,030
However, Emiya...

205
00:13:54,610 --> 00:13:58,780
Are Caster's actions
really so terrible?

206
00:13:59,320 --> 00:14:01,869
What... did you say?

207
00:14:01,870 --> 00:14:06,120
The deaths of strangers, no matter
the number, are of no concern to me.

208
00:14:06,410 --> 00:14:10,629
Just as they are not the least
bit concerned about my life.

209
00:14:10,630 --> 00:14:12,209
Kuzuki...

210
00:14:12,210 --> 00:14:15,710
You're a mage, but
you'd involve outsiders?

211
00:14:16,420 --> 00:14:18,720
I am no mage.

212
00:14:19,130 --> 00:14:21,970
I'm simply a killer who's a
mere shadow of his former self.

213
00:14:22,800 --> 00:14:25,849
I will not participate
in the Holy Grail War.

214
00:14:25,850 --> 00:14:28,335
Whether Caster kills
people or you all fight

215
00:14:28,347 --> 00:14:30,730
to the death, I will
do nothing but watch.

216
00:14:31,190 --> 00:14:34,980
I will bear no responsibility
for your fighting,

217
00:14:35,690 --> 00:14:39,490
and neither should any of you
bear responsibility for my life.

218
00:14:40,410 --> 00:14:42,740
Do as you wish, Caster.

219
00:14:43,320 --> 00:14:46,370
Whether you let them
live or kill them is up to you.

220
00:14:47,620 --> 00:14:48,959
I see.

221
00:14:48,960 --> 00:14:51,250
Then you have no
qualms about dying here,

222
00:14:51,750 --> 00:14:53,170
Master of Caster?

223
00:14:57,710 --> 00:14:58,710
Saber!

224
00:15:08,980 --> 00:15:10,730
Not so fast, Saber.

225
00:15:14,150 --> 00:15:15,360
Magic resistance?

226
00:15:16,110 --> 00:15:17,230
Souichirou-sama!

227
00:15:30,120 --> 00:15:32,040
You underestimate me, Saber!

228
00:15:51,140 --> 00:15:53,769
His fists have been
fortified with magic?

229
00:15:53,770 --> 00:15:55,649
You evade well.

230
00:15:55,650 --> 00:15:57,690
Ah. So it is not your
eyes that are keen

231
00:15:58,320 --> 00:16:00,230
but your intuition.

232
00:16:24,720 --> 00:16:27,179
That's not possible.

233
00:16:27,180 --> 00:16:31,220
It's fine to assume that a Master's
role is to provide rear support.

234
00:16:31,720 --> 00:16:34,389
But there is an
exception to every rule.

235
00:16:34,390 --> 00:16:39,480
There are also Masters, like me,
that can only fight on the front line.

236
00:16:42,030 --> 00:16:43,030
Master...

237
00:16:43,650 --> 00:16:45,240
What is it, Caster?

238
00:16:45,660 --> 00:16:48,449
I shall handle Saber.

239
00:16:48,450 --> 00:16:50,490
You see to the other Masters.

240
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:52,080
Very well.

241
00:16:53,750 --> 00:16:54,830
Suits me.

242
00:16:55,330 --> 00:16:57,709
You caught Saber by surprise,

243
00:16:57,710 --> 00:17:00,670
but we just need to take
you out before you get close.

244
00:17:14,980 --> 00:17:16,730
Tohsaka!

245
00:17:33,660 --> 00:17:35,499
If I go down,

246
00:17:35,500 --> 00:17:37,040
Tohsaka's dead.

247
00:17:39,670 --> 00:17:41,340
I can't let that happen.

248
00:17:42,380 --> 00:17:43,380
Weapons...

249
00:17:43,960 --> 00:17:46,130
I need weapons
that will let me fight.

250
00:17:47,720 --> 00:17:49,840
Powerful weapons.

251
00:17:50,930 --> 00:17:54,850
Like the ones he had.

252
00:17:58,060 --> 00:18:00,310
Trace on!

253
00:18:32,930 --> 00:18:33,930
No way.

254
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:42,100
Those are...

255
00:18:44,480 --> 00:18:45,570
Master!

256
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:50,030
Saber...

257
00:18:57,120 --> 00:18:57,750
Wait.

258
00:18:58,120 --> 00:18:59,409
That's enough.

259
00:18:59,410 --> 00:19:01,000
Withdraw, Caster.

260
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,000
As you wish.

261
00:19:15,010 --> 00:19:16,639
Shirou, are you injured?

262
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:18,269
Saber...

263
00:19:18,270 --> 00:19:19,390
We blew it.

264
00:19:20,980 --> 00:19:24,190
Now, Kuzuki won't set foot
outside of Ryuudou Temple.

265
00:19:24,940 --> 00:19:28,229
You mean to give up
on slaying Caster, then?

266
00:19:28,230 --> 00:19:29,439
You must be joking.

267
00:19:29,440 --> 00:19:31,150
We can't let her run loose.

268
00:19:31,490 --> 00:19:32,910
Of course we can't.

269
00:19:35,410 --> 00:19:38,659
Anyway, Emiya-kun,
what were those?

270
00:19:38,660 --> 00:19:41,580
I thought that fortification magic
was the only type you could do.

271
00:19:41,960 --> 00:19:46,129
Well, it is. But projection was
the first type I succeeded at.

272
00:19:46,130 --> 00:19:49,379
It ticks me off that you only
thought to mention this now.

273
00:19:49,380 --> 00:19:52,340
So you're saying this
wasn't your first time?

274
00:19:53,090 --> 00:19:55,089
I guess not.

275
00:19:55,090 --> 00:19:57,139
But I could only mimic
the appearances of things.

276
00:19:57,140 --> 00:19:59,429
Inside, they were always hollow.

277
00:19:59,430 --> 00:20:02,850
That's why I'm as surprised
as you with what happened.

278
00:20:03,190 --> 00:20:06,859
You picked up projection
before fortification?

279
00:20:06,860 --> 00:20:08,860
Look, that was all I could do.

280
00:20:09,440 --> 00:20:11,267
Kiritsugu said it was
totally useless in that

281
00:20:11,279 --> 00:20:13,200
state and that I should
focus on fortification.

282
00:20:13,780 --> 00:20:15,029
I suppose so.

283
00:20:15,030 --> 00:20:17,030
I probably would
have said the same.

284
00:20:17,870 --> 00:20:20,370
Still, it's awfully strange.

285
00:20:21,250 --> 00:20:22,250
Tohsaka?

286
00:20:23,210 --> 00:20:24,290
Let's go home.

287
00:20:28,590 --> 00:20:29,590
Shirou!

288
00:20:31,630 --> 00:20:32,840
I'm fine.

289
00:20:45,900 --> 00:20:48,730
Oh, so this is where you were?

290
00:20:49,110 --> 00:20:52,859
Don't worry. I'm
not here to complain.

291
00:20:52,860 --> 00:20:55,990
I don't care where
you go or what you do.

292
00:20:56,610 --> 00:20:59,659
But listen to this.
I have great news!

293
00:20:59,660 --> 00:21:04,289
Kotomine says he'll turn a
blind eye to anything we do.

294
00:21:04,290 --> 00:21:08,169
He seems to think
rather highly of you.

295
00:21:08,170 --> 00:21:11,799
Well, he's a good
judge of people.

296
00:21:11,800 --> 00:21:16,180
I'm thinking of giving him something as
a token of thanks once we get the Grail.

297
00:21:16,590 --> 00:21:19,639
So we should start
killing everyone in sight.

298
00:21:19,640 --> 00:21:22,679
Eat up souls, and
make yourself stronger!

299
00:21:22,680 --> 00:21:26,190
And then it'll be their turn!

300
00:21:27,020 --> 00:21:31,770
I gotta settle the score
with Emiya, you know?

301
00:21:36,150 --> 00:21:40,870
Shinji, you fail to comprehend
the Grail's true nature.

302
00:21:43,580 --> 00:21:48,539
If you truly desire the Grail,
ignore the other Masters.

303
00:21:48,540 --> 00:21:51,540
They are naught
more than sacrifices.

304
00:21:52,340 --> 00:21:55,629
There are other matters
that must be attended to first.

305
00:21:55,630 --> 00:21:57,760
Attended to?

306
00:21:58,220 --> 00:22:01,390
I am not unsympathetic
to your feelings, however.

307
00:22:02,050 --> 00:22:04,639
Revenge feels divine.

308
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:07,270
To seek pleasure is
proof of being human.

309
00:22:08,140 --> 00:22:10,600
Once I have done
what needs to be done,

310
00:22:11,360 --> 00:22:14,020
I shall join in your games.

311
00:22:16,190 --> 00:22:20,530
C-Come to think of it, I never
asked what your wish was, did I?

312
00:22:22,910 --> 00:22:25,540
I approve of luxury.

313
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:29,250
Extravagant decoration
is to be admired above all.

314
00:22:29,960 --> 00:22:33,629
But there is no sense in
wasting that upon the superfluous.

315
00:22:33,630 --> 00:22:35,420
The superfluous?

316
00:22:36,050 --> 00:22:39,129
Long ago, I selected ten slaves,

317
00:22:39,130 --> 00:22:42,930
with the intent of slaying
one that would not be missed.

318
00:22:43,970 --> 00:22:46,140
What do you suppose
happened, Shinji?

319
00:22:47,980 --> 00:22:50,060
You killed them all, right?

320
00:22:52,230 --> 00:22:55,229
I found that I could
not slay any of them.

321
00:22:55,230 --> 00:23:00,200
They were simple laborers, but in
the old world, none were without value.

322
00:23:02,240 --> 00:23:06,199
But this world overflows
with the superfluous.

323
00:23:06,200 --> 00:23:09,409
I could choose not
only ten but thousands

324
00:23:09,410 --> 00:23:12,080
and I'd not find a single one
amongst them that I could not kill.

325
00:23:13,380 --> 00:23:17,549
I don't get what you're
saying. What is it that you want?

326
00:23:17,550 --> 00:23:19,130
That is simple.

327
00:23:19,880 --> 00:23:23,890
Too many of
anything is sickening.

328
00:23:40,450 --> 00:23:46,589
We didn't understand anything

329
00:23:46,590 --> 00:23:52,759
My left hand groped for
things that vanished to my touch

330
00:23:52,760 --> 00:23:55,759
A moral conflict

331
00:23:55,760 --> 00:23:58,560
stays your hand

332
00:23:58,810 --> 00:24:01,309
and tricks you

333
00:24:01,310 --> 00:24:03,190
out of your future

334
00:24:03,440 --> 00:24:10,109
I don't know how
to protect anyone,

335
00:24:10,110 --> 00:24:15,910
and my ideals might
well be pointless,

336
00:24:16,120 --> 00:24:24,120
but I want to live my life

337
00:24:25,120 --> 00:24:30,129
The past repeats before my eyes

338
00:24:30,130 --> 00:24:37,929
Here I will trust the me
that now stands with you

339
00:24:37,930 --> 00:24:44,019
Until my dream
crumbles and withers,

340
00:24:44,020 --> 00:24:49,649
I hope you will carve
out paradise with me

341
00:24:49,650 --> 00:24:53,360
Fight your fate

342
00:24:56,850 --> 00:24:58,729
I've opened something
that was once closed?

343
00:24:58,730 --> 00:25:01,689
If you come any closer, I hope you're
prepared to face the consequences.

344
00:25:01,690 --> 00:25:04,069
Tomorrow, I'll make
you admit defeat!

345
00:25:04,070 --> 00:25:07,199
I wanted to be a champion
of justice, just like Kiritsugu.

346
00:25:07,200 --> 00:25:10,280
That is why your
ideals are meaningless.

347
00:25:07,240 --> 00:25:09,160
A Visitor Approaches Lightly

348
00:25:09,161 --> 00:25:11,080
Next Time

